Topic : Why .dockerignore ?

>Without .dockerignore:
All files in your directory, even large or irrelevant ones, get sent to the Docker daemon, slowing down builds.

>With .dockerignore:
Only the necessary files are copied, making the image smaller, faster to build, and more secure.

Sample File :-

# Ignore Git and node modules
.git
node_modules

# Logs
*.log

# Environment files
.env
*.env

# OS or IDE files
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Build artifacts
dist/
build/

Importance of .dockerignore :-

1.Reduces Image Size
	•	By ignoring unnecessary files (e.g., .git, node_modules, logs)

2.	Improves Build Performance
	•	Docker doesn’t waste time copying or processing files that aren’t needed.

3.	Protects Sensitive Information
	•	Prevents secrets like .env, private keys,credentials from being included.

4.	Avoids Cache Busting
	•	Unchanging but frequently updated files (like logs or temp files) can invalidate build cache if not ignored.
